---
import CaseStudyLayout from '../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro';
import InsightCallout from '../../components/InsightCallout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import BeforeAfter from '../../components/BeforeAfter.astro';
import FullWidthImage from '../../components/FullWidthImage.astro';

import thumbnail from '../../assets/images/projects/leadsuite/thumbnail.png';
import personPageOld from '../../assets/images/projects/leadsuite/Person-page-old.png';
import personProfileNew from '../../assets/images/projects/leadsuite/person-profile-new.png';
import caseDetail from '../../assets/images/projects/leadsuite/case-detail.png';
import caseDetailTimelineMap from '../../assets/images/projects/leadsuite/case-detail-timeline-map.png';
import leadReviewPerson from '../../assets/images/projects/leadsuite/lead-review-person.png';
import dashboardPropertyPanel from '../../assets/images/projects/leadsuite/dashboard-property-panel.png';
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="LeadSuite"
  description="LeadSuite is the flagship product at LeadsOnline, a B2B SaaS platform used by law enforcement to work cases and surface insights. I led the redesign of the core person profile and case detail experience, turning an information-dense legacy interface into a structured, scalable investigative tool."
  tags={['B2B SaaS', 'Law Enforcement', 'Information Architecture']}
  heroImage={thumbnail}
  slug="leadsuite"
  accentColor="#1c3557"
  previousProject={{ title: 'GriefShare', slug: 'griefshare' }}
  nextProject={{ title: 'Deposify', slug: 'deposify' }}
>
  <div class="case-study-body">

    <div class="container">
      <p class="disclaimer">*This work involves sensitive law-enforcement investigations, so I can't share full details publicly. These visuals are representative of the live product, and I'm glad to walk through the complete case study and design decisions in conversation.*</p>
    </div>

    <!-- Challenge -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading
          title="The Challenge"
          subtitle="LeadSuite was originally a quick reskin of a low-adoption legacy product, carrying over its structure with no rethink of investigative workflows or modern UX patterns. A UX audit before touching anything confirmed the full scope: a person profile with no structure, and a case detail view that made it hard to follow the thread of an investigation."
        />
        <p class="design-question"><strong>Design Question:</strong> How do you redesign a tool investigators rely on daily so the disruption makes them faster, not just more comfortable?</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Pain Points -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading title="What We Were Up Against" />
        <div class="insights-grid">
          <InsightCallout
            title="Wall of noise"
            description="The person profile loaded every data point simultaneously with no visual hierarchy. Investigators had to scan the entire page to find what they needed, with no tabbed structure, no grouping, no clear entry point."
          />
          <InsightCallout
            title="Hard to follow, harder to discover"
            description="The original timeline and map design required cumbersome dual-axis scrolling to navigate. Enough functionality was buried or unclear that investigators, including me during the audit, were missing it entirely."
          />
          <InsightCallout
            title="Vague requirements"
            description="PM asks were directional, not defined. 'Make it easier to use' was the brief. I used the audit findings as a foundation, then facilitated team discussions to translate directional asks into specific, buildable decisions."
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Person Profile -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading
          title="Person Profile"
          subtitle="The redesign introduces a tabbed structure - Cases, Associates, Activity Log, and a new 'Deep Background' tab that consolidates public records, criminal history, and other investigative data sources into one view. Each tab gives investigators a direct path to what they need instead of forcing them to scan the entire page."
        />
        <BeforeAfter
          beforeImage={personPageOld}
          afterImage={personProfileNew}
          beforeLabel="Before"
          afterLabel="After"
          beforeAlt="Original LeadSuite person page with flat layout"
          afterAlt="Redesigned person profile with tabbed navigation and organized sections"
        />
        <p class="pull-quote">The redesigned person profile now drives over 50% of all traffic in the app.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Case Detail Overview -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading
          title="Case Detail"
          subtitle="The case detail page is where investigators spend most of their time. I restructured it around a vertical navigation with distinct views: an overview with the case summary and map, a timeline and map view for spatial-temporal analysis, and an evidence tab. Each view serves a different mode of investigative thinking without cluttering the others."
        />
        <FullWidthImage
          src={caseDetail}
          alt="Redesigned case detail overview showing case summary, leads cards, and map"
          caption="Case detail overview: summary narrative, leads cards, and geographic context in one view"
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Timeline + Map -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading
          title="Timeline + Map"
          subtitle="I redesigned the timeline as a full-width horizontal view, synced to the map, so investigators get two representations of the same facts for two different ways of thinking through a case. Events scroll chronologically left to right, and selecting one highlights its location on the map below."
        />
        <FullWidthImage
          src={caseDetailTimelineMap}
          alt="Case detail timeline and map view with narrative events synced to geographic locations"
          caption="Timeline + Map: narrative events synced to geographic locations for spatial-temporal analysis"
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Leads -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading
          title="Leads"
          subtitle="Leads is a net new feature, built in close collaboration with one of the developers. He brought the concept, and we workshopped it together until it became a focused workspace where investigators could track threads tied to a case, separate from the raw data views. It's designed to feel like a working surface, not a report."
        />
        <FullWidthImage
          src={leadReviewPerson}
          alt="Lead review modal showing a person of interest with investigative leads and intel connections"
          caption="Lead review: surfacing proximity, timing, and cross-case connections for a person of interest"
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What's Next -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading
          title="What's Next"
          subtitle='The redesign launched first to beta users, then expanded to a controlled subset of existing LeadsOnline customers, with a full rollout weeks away. Alongside the core redesign, two new features are in active design: a Dashboard surfacing personalized investigative activity and trend detection, and an AI-powered search. The vision for where these features lead is covered in <a href="/projects/unified-platform">Unifying an Investigative Platform</a>.'
        />
        <FullWidthImage
          src={dashboardPropertyPanel}
          alt="LeadSuite dashboard with analytics, trends, and property intelligence panel"
          caption="Dashboard with property intelligence panel: personalized activity, analytics, and trend detection"
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Reflection -->
    <section class="case-section section">
      <div class="container">
        <SectionHeading title="Reflection" />
        <div class="reflections-grid">
          <div class="reflection-item">
            <h3>Real usage, real validation</h3>
            <p>The redesigned person profile now drives over 50% of all traffic in the app. That signal confirmed the tabbed structure was solving a real navigation problem, not just a visual one.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="reflection-item">
            <h3>Scalable structure pays off</h3>
            <p>The tabbed model has already absorbed two new data source integrations without touching the core layout. Building for growth wasn't over-engineering, it was the right call given the product roadmap.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="reflection-item">
            <h3>Ambiguity is a design surface</h3>
            <p>The vaguest asks often point to the most important problems. "Make it easier to use" turned into a full information architecture rethink.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>
</CaseStudyLayout>

<script>
  import { initCaseStudyAnimations } from '../../scripts/scroll-animations';
  import { initScrollVelocityParallax } from '../../scripts/hover-effects';
  document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', () => {
    if (!window.location.pathname.startsWith('/projects/leadsuite')) return;
    initCaseStudyAnimations('.case-section');
    initScrollVelocityParallax();
  });
</script>
